# Adversarial Verification Harness

**Default: work freely.** Full harness is **opt-in**.

| Mode | When | Approach |
|---|---|---|
| Free (default) | Everyday work; no active harness task | Just do it. No planner/contract required. |
| Opt-in full harness | User says `use harness` / `with harness`, or launches `/planner` / skill `adversarial-harness` | Planner → contract → build → `/evaluator` |
| Resume | Active task (`pending`/`building`/`evaluating`) | Continue negotiate → build → verify |

- Idle harness (no state, or only committed/cancelled/verified) → free writes.
- Active harness → need `.harness/contract.json` before impl (hooks deny ungated writes).
- Do not self-certify → `/evaluator` PASS before `verified: true`.
- Multi-file harness work → TodoWrite + breadcrumb in `.harness/breadcrumbs.jsonl`.
- Say `skip harness` to cancel an opt-in arm / leave active mode.

Roles: `/planner` (vision, max 5 tasks, no code) · Builder (contract + impl) · `/evaluator` (negotiate + verify; `.harness/` only).

Procedure: skill `adversarial-harness`. Design: `docs/HARNESS_ESSENCE.md`.
